What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/20700008.reboot-mode/next_mode
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	whatshu <shussm@qq.com>
Description:
		Select the ESP32-S31 boot path for the next orderly system restart.
		Read or write "normal" (default) or "bootloader". Only root can
		write this attribute. Other values return EINVAL.

		The value is kept in RAM until the reboot notifier runs. Selecting
		bootloader does not reset the board or write flash. Shutdown and
		poweroff do not apply it. A RESTART2 command, when supplied,
		takes precedence over the saved value.

		Bootloader selects the ROM UART/USB downloader. Before resetting
		back into the application, the flashing tool must clear bit 2 of
		LP_SYSTEM control at 0x20700008; the bit survives a software reset.
Users:		ESP-Mosaico /sbin/reboot wrapper for BusyBox init
